    Let~$G$ be a simple Lie group and let~$P$ be a parabolic subgroup of~$G$. Then:

    \begin{enumerate}
        \item If~$G/P$ admits proper almost-homogeneous domains, then it is an irreducible Nagano space.

        \item If~$G/P$ is an irreducible Nagano space~$N$, and if it is neither Example (ix) nor (iv, $\min(p,q)=1$) of Table~\ref{table_nagano_full}, then any proper almost-homogeneous domain of~$N$ is a realization of~$\mathbb{X}(N)$, and is in particular symmetric.
    \end{enumerate}

