    \item Let $L$ be a type-B Ordovician lattice corresponding to $\overrightarrow{B}$, and let $i\in L$ be an atom. Then $\mu_i(L)$ corresponds to the quiver $\mu_i(\overrightarrow{B})$. Here, the correspondence between an Ordovician lattice and a quiver in the above statements is given by \cref{type-B Cambrian lattice and ideal polygon}.
  \end{enumerate}

