  \!\left(2d - \sum_{i=1}^{d}( e^{2\pi  i\theta_d} +e^{-2\pi  i\theta_d} ) - E \right)^s
  \frac{d\theta_1\cdots d\theta_d}{(2\pi)^d}.
\end{equation}

Instead of ${\rm Tr}$ or $\det$ one can put any other function and a similar equality is expected. In other words, moments and entire spectral measure with appropriate normalization
tend to the one of the lattice.

